# CNAME — put your custom domain here (one line, no protocol).
# When deploying to GitHub Pages, this file tells GH to serve
# the site at your custom domain instead of <username>.github.io.
#
# Examples:
#   videolearning.app
#   www.videolearning.app
#   learn.yourdomain.com
#
# If you're using the default <username>.github.io URL, just delete this file.
#
# IMPORTANT: After enabling, also configure DNS at your registrar:
#   - CNAME record: www → <username>.github.io
#   - A records for apex (no www):
#       185.199.108.153
#       185.199.109.153
#       185.199.110.153
#       185.199.111.153
# Then in GitHub → Settings → Pages → Custom domain, enter the domain
# and enable "Enforce HTTPS".
